<title>BELGIUM: Belgian PM wants Blair to make success of EU's IGC.</title>
<headline>Belgian PM wants Blair to make success of EU's IGC.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Prime Minister Jean-Luc Dehaene, the man blocked by John Major from becoming the European Union Commission's president, on Friday welcomed Tony Blair's election as Britain's prime minister, adding he hoped Blair would make a success of the EU's future.</p>
<p>&quot;In this crucial phase of common challenges, I am looking forward to new cooperation with you and our (EU) colleagues to make a success of the (EU's) inter-governmental conference and the building of a strengthened Euro-Atlantic relationship,&quot; Deheane said in a statement issued through the Belga news agency.</p>
</text>
